    <p class="title is-5 mathjax">
      
        Can We Predict the Unpredictable? Leveraging DisasterNet-LLM for Multimodal Disaster Classification
      
    </p>
    <p class="authors">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Authors:</span>
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Kulahara%2C+M">Manaswi Kulahara</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Kashyap%2C+G+S">Gautam Siddharth Kashyap</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Joshi%2C+N">Nipun Joshi</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Soni%2C+A">Arpita Soni</a>
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="search-hit">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2506.23462v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        &hellip;methods struggle to integrate multimodal data such as images, weather records, and textual reports. To address this, we propose DisasterNet-LLM, a specialized Large <span class="search-hit mathjax">Language</span>&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2506.23462v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2506.23462v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2506.23462v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        Effective disaster management requires timely and accurate insights, yet traditional methods struggle to integrate multimodal data such as images, weather records, and textual reports. To address this, we propose DisasterNet-LLM, a specialized Large <span class="search-hit mathjax">Language</span> <span class="search-hit mathjax">Model</span> (LLM) designed for comprehensive disaster analysis. By leveraging advanced pretraining, cross-modal attention mechanisms, and adaptive transformers, DisasterNet-LLM excels in disaster classification. Experimental results demonstrate its superiority over state-of-the-art <span class="search-hit mathjax">models</span>, achieving higher accuracy of 89.5%, an F1 score of 88.0%, AUC of 0.92%, and BERTScore of 0.88% in multimodal disaster classification tasks.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2506.23462v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2506.23462v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

    <p class="is-size-7"><span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Submitted</span> 29 June, 2025; 
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">originally announced</span> June 2025.
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="comments is-size-7">
